{% comment %}
  ==================================================================
  GS TOKEN BRIDGE
  ==================================================================
  Maps gs-shopify-v3 design tokens onto Dawn's native token system so
  ported v3 sections render correctly without rewriting their CSS.

  INSTALL: add this line to layout/theme.liquid immediately AFTER the
  closing endstyle tag of Dawn's own style block:

      render 'gs-token-bridge'

  It must come after Dawn's style block because it reads the Dawn
  variables defined there.

  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  REVISION 2026-08-11 (second pass)
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  The first version used placeholder values for every token Dawn has no
  equivalent for. Those are now REAL, read from v3 config/settings_data.json
  on the live theme. Source values are cited inline.

  Confirmed brand facts from settings_data.json:
    Type      Roboto Condensed - headings n5 (500), body n4 (400)
    Scale     heading 28px desktop / 22px mobile
              body 16px desktop / 13px mobile
    Red       #ab192d  (buttons, links, sale/new/preorder/custom badges, errors)
    Header    #000000 bg, #ffffff text, #e7e7e7 hover, #5c5c5c cart count
    Footer    #000000 bg, #ffffff text, #a6a6a6 links
    Stock     in #002F6E (navy), low #ab192d, out #777777
    Rating    #9a723f (bronze)
    Success   #2c7e3f
    RADII     ALL ZERO. Square corners everywhere. button_radius is false,
              and product/image/input/card radii are 0 on desktop AND mobile.
    Buttons   uppercase, no shadow (enable_button_shadow false)

  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  WHY A BRIDGE INSTEAD OF PORTING style-variables.liquid
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Dawn already defines a complete scheme system. Porting v3's file would
  create a second, competing one. The bridge aliases v3 names to Dawn's
  values so a ported section keeps working, while Dawn's own sections
  stay on Dawn's names. One source of truth, two vocabularies.

  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  SCHEME CLASS MISMATCH - IMPORTANT
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Dawn emits  .color-{scheme.id}
  v3 emitted  .scheme-{scheme.id}
  Ported markup using class="scheme-x" would match nothing. The alias
  block below makes .scheme-* work. The correct long-term fix is
  updating ported markup to Dawn's .color-* convention.

  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  BUGS FIXED IN TRANSIT (do not reintroduce)
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  1. --alternateButtonBorder was "25,,255,255" in BOTH v3 dark-mode
     blocks. Double comma = invalid CSS = property silently dropped.
  2. --line-color was 4 components in light mode (r,g,b,1) and 3 in
     dark. Standardised to 3; use rgba(var(--line-color), alpha).
  3. --overlayColor was an RGB triplet in light mode and the hex #000
     in dark, so rgb(var(--overlayColor)) broke in dark mode.
  4. v3 tested colour settings with "!= empty"; "blank" is correct.

  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  STILL OPEN
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
  These are hardcoded brand constants, not merchant-editable settings.
  Before launch each needs a real entry in settings_schema.json so the
  team can change them without a developer: the header token set, the
  five badge colour pairs, and the stock-status colours.

  DARK MODE is not carried over. v3 shipped a dark mode whose colours
  were hardcoded rather than derived from schemes, so changing a colour
  scheme in v3 has no effect in dark mode today. Dawn has no native dark
  mode. Rebuilding it is a decision, not a port - and v3's setting
  enable_dl_mode_toggle is currently false, so nothing is lost by
  omitting it.
  ==================================================================
{% endcomment %}

{% style %}
  /* ---------------------------------------------------------------
     1. SCHEME ALIASES
     v3 token names re-declared against Dawn's per-scheme values.
     --------------------------------------------------------------- */
  {%- for scheme in settings.color_schemes -%}
    {%- if forloop.first -%}:root,{%- endif %}
    .color-{{ scheme.id }},
    .scheme-{{ scheme.id }} {
      /* Dawn ships RGB triplets and so did v3, so these pass through. */
      --background: var(--color-background);
      --gradientBackground: var(--gradient-background);
      --alternateBackground: var(--color-background-contrast);
      --textColor: var(--color-foreground);
      --linkColor: var(--color-link);

      /* Dawn has no separate heading colour. v3 did. */
      --headingColor: var(--color-foreground);

      --buttonBackground: var(--color-button);
      --buttonColor: var(--color-button-text);
      --buttonBorder: var(--color-button);

      /* Dawn has no hover scheme colours. v3 primary hover was #8a1424,
         a darker red. Inverted default here; override per scheme if the
         visual diff shows it matters. */
      --buttonBackgroundHover: var(--color-button-text);
      --buttonColorHover: var(--color-button);
      --buttonBorderHover: var(--color-button);

      --alternateButtonBackground: var(--color-secondary-button);
      --alternateButtonColor: var(--color-secondary-button-text);
      /* FIXED: v3 had "25,,255,255" here - double comma, invalid. */
      --alternateButtonBorder: var(--color-secondary-button-text);
      --alternateButtonBackgroundHover: var(--color-secondary-button-text);
      --alternateButtonColorHover: var(--color-secondary-button);
      --alternateButtonBorderHover: var(--color-secondary-button-text);

      --inputBackground: var(--color-background);
      --inputColor: var(--color-foreground);
      --inputBorder: var(--color-foreground);

      --cardBackground: var(--color-background);
      --productBorder: var(--color-foreground);
      --borderColor: var(--color-foreground);
      --shadowColor: var(--color-shadow);

      --sliderArrowBackground: var(--color-foreground);
      --sliderArrowColor: var(--color-background);

      --highlightTextColor: rgb(var(--color-foreground));
      --highlightGradientBackground: var(--gradient-background);
      --highlightBackground: var(--color-background);
      --cardDetailsTextColor: var(--color-foreground);
      --productImagebackground: rgb(var(--color-background));
    }
  {%- endfor %}

  /* ---------------------------------------------------------------
     2. GLOBAL GS TOKENS
     Values below are the real v3 settings, not placeholders.
     --------------------------------------------------------------- */
  :root {
    /* Typography. v3: roboto_condensed_n5 headings / n4 body. Set the
       same fonts in Dawn's theme settings and these track them. */
    --bodyFont: var(--font-body-family);
    --bodyFontWeight: var(--font-body-weight);
    --bodyFontStyle: var(--font-body-style);
    --headingFont: var(--font-heading-family);
    --headingFontWeight: var(--font-heading-weight);
    --headingFontStyle: var(--font-heading-style);
    --buttonFont: var(--font-body-family);
    --buttonFontWeight: var(--font-heading-weight);
    --buttonFontStyle: var(--font-body-style);

    /* v3 scale: body 13px mobile / 16px desktop,
                 heading 22px mobile / 28px desktop. */
    --bodyFontBase: 1.3rem;
    --headingFontBase: 2.2rem;
    --bodyFontLineHeight: 1.5;
    --headingFontLineHeight: 1.2;

    --xsmallText: calc(var(--bodyFontBase) - 0.4rem);
    --smallText: calc(var(--bodyFontBase) - 0.2rem);
    --text: var(--bodyFontBase);
    --mediumText: calc(var(--bodyFontBase) + 0.2rem);
    --largeText: calc(var(--bodyFontBase) + 0.4rem);
    --xlargeText: calc(var(--bodyFontBase) + 0.6rem);

    /* v3 mobile heading scale offsets. */
    --h0: calc(var(--headingFontBase) + 1rem);
    --h1: calc(var(--headingFontBase) + 0.8rem);
    --h2: calc(var(--headingFontBase) + 0.2rem);
    --h3: var(--headingFontBase);
    --h4: calc(var(--headingFontBase) - 0.2rem);
    --h5: calc(var(--headingFontBase) - 0.4rem);
    --h6: calc(var(--headingFontBase) - 0.6rem);

    /* RADII - all zero in v3. button_radius is false; product, image,
       input and card radii are 0 on both breakpoints. Square corners
       are a deliberate brand choice, not an oversight. */
    --buttonRadius: 0;
    --inputRadius: 0;
    --imageRadius: 0;
    --cardRadius: 0;
    --productRadius: 0;
    --gs-swatch-radius: 50%;

    /* v3 button_text_transform: uppercase, enable_button_shadow: false */
    --buttonText: uppercase;
    --buttonShadow: transparent;
    --secondaryButtonShadow: transparent;

    --img-square: 100%;
    --img-portrait: 130%;
    --img-landscape: 75%;
    --imageFit: cover;
    --imageRatio: 0%;
    --marqueeSpeed: 3s;
    --sliderArrowWidth: 44px;

    /* FIXED: standardised to a 3-component triplet. Use as
       rgba(var(--line-color), 1). v3 primary highlight_color #ffca10;
       quaternary used #ab192d. Brand red chosen as the global default. */
    --line-color: 171,25,45;

    /* FIXED: was a triplet in light mode and #000 in dark. */
    --overlayColor: 0,0,0;
    --overlayText: #ffffff;
    --overlayBackground: 0,0,0;
    --overlayOpacity: 0.4;
    --bg-blur: 0px;

    /* Status colours - v3 success_message / error_message. */
    --success: 44,126,63;    /* #2c7e3f */
    --error: 171,25,45;      /* #ab192d */

    /* Badge colours - v3 saleBadgeBg / newBadgeBg / preorderBadgeBg /
       customBadgeBg were ALL #ab192d. Sold-out has no v3 setting; grey
       chosen. Foreground computed the way v3 did it: white on anything
       darker than mid-brightness. */
    --saleBadgeBackground: 171,25,45;
    --saleBadgeColor: #ffffff;
    --newBadgeBackground: 171,25,45;
    --newBadgeColor: #ffffff;
    --preorderBadgeBackground: 171,25,45;
    --preorderBadgeColor: #ffffff;
    --soldBadgeBackground: 92,92,92;
    --soldBadgeColor: #ffffff;
    --customBadgeBackground: 171,25,45;
    --customBadgeColor: #ffffff;
    --discount-background: #ab192d;
    --discount-color: #ffffff;

    /* v3 rating_color #9a723f - bronze, not the usual gold. */
    --ratingStarColor: 154,114,63;

    /* Stock status - v3 product_in_stock_color / product_low_stock_color.
       In-stock is navy #002F6E, NOT green. */
    --instock-text: #002F6E;
    --outofstock-text: #777777;
    --lowstock-text: #ab192d;

    /* HEADER - v3 background_header #000000, header_text #ffffff,
       header_text_hover #e7e7e7, header_icon #ffffff,
       header_cart_count_bg #5c5c5c, search_input_color #000000.
       No Dawn equivalent; these are literals until wired to settings. */
    --headerBg: #000000;
    --headerColor: #ffffff;
    --headerHoverColor: #e7e7e7;
    --headerIconColor: #ffffff;
    --transparentHeaderColor: #ffffff;
    --cartCountBg: #5c5c5c;
    --cartCountColor: #ffffff;
    --submenuBg: #000000;
    --submenuColor: #ffffff;
    --submenuHoverColor: #e7e7e7;
    --submenutwoBg: #000000;
    --submenutwoColor: #ffffff;
    --submenutwoHoverColor: #e7e7e7;
    --searchTextColor: #000000;
    --searchBackgroundColor: #ffffff;
    --backToTopBackground: #000000;
    --backToTopColor: #ffffff;
  }

  /* v3 secondary_background_header #000000 / text #ffffff. */
  .secondary-header,
  #hamburger-menu,
  #hamburger-menu-wrapper {
    --headerBg: #000000;
    --headerColor: #ffffff;
    --headerHoverColor: #ffffff;
  }

  /* ---------------------------------------------------------------
     3. CUSTOM SWATCH COLOURS
     Ported from v3's settings.custom_colors parser, guarded against
     malformed lines. Uses image_url; v3 used deprecated file_img_url.
     --------------------------------------------------------------- */
  {%- if settings.custom_colors != blank -%}
    {%- assign customColors = settings.custom_colors | newline_to_br | split: '<br />' -%}
    {%- for color in customColors -%}
      {%- assign pair = color | strip | split: ':' -%}
      {%- if pair.size >= 2 -%}
        {%- assign swatchName = pair.first | strip -%}
        {%- assign swatchValue = pair.last | strip -%}
        {%- if swatchName != blank and swatchValue != blank -%}
          [data-color="{{ swatchName }}"] {
            {%- if swatchValue contains '#' -%}
              background-color: {{ swatchValue }} !important;
            {%- else -%}
              background-image: url({{ swatchValue | image_url: width: 100 }}) !important;
            {%- endif -%}
          }
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  {%- endif -%}

  /* ---------------------------------------------------------------
     4. DESKTOP SCALE
     v3 body_scale_desktop 16 / heading_font_scale_desktop 28.
     --------------------------------------------------------------- */
  @media (min-width: 750px) {
    :root {
      --bodyFontBase: 1.6rem;
      --headingFontBase: 2.8rem;
      --h0: calc(var(--headingFontBase) + 3.2rem);
      --h1: calc(var(--headingFontBase) + 1.9rem);
      --h2: calc(var(--headingFontBase) + 0.4rem);
      --h4: calc(var(--headingFontBase) - 0.4rem);
      --h5: calc(var(--headingFontBase) - 0.6rem);
      --h6: calc(var(--headingFontBase) - 0.8rem);
    }
  }
{% endstyle %}
